Scene One 
The Prophecy No One Heard
Not every night is measured by the passing of hours.
Some drift through human history like a warm summer breeze, leaving behind nothing more than a fading memory.
Others become the moments when history quietly changes its course forever—
while the world sleeps peacefully, unaware that the future has already begun to write itself.
This was one of those nights.
The summer of 1956.
In Hanover, New Hampshire, heavy clouds blanketed the night sky as a gentle rain tapped against the windows in a rhythm that echoed like the whispers of time itself. The wind swept through the ancient trees surrounding Dartmouth College, stirring their branches as though nature were preparing to witness an event unlike anything humanity had ever known.
Silence settled across the campus.
Most of the buildings had gone dark. Classroom doors were locked, students had returned home, and the only sounds that remained were the soft rainfall and the measured footsteps of the night watchman making his rounds along the old stone walkways.
He walked slowly, his wooden staff striking the ground with quiet familiarity.
Then something caught his attention.
At the end of a long corridor, a thin ribbon of light slipped from beneath the door of a lecture room—as if it had refused to surrender to the night.
The watchman stopped.
For a brief moment, he stared at the glowing line beneath the door before smiling to himself and gently shaking his head.
"Those professors..." he murmured. "I don't think they know the meaning of rest."
He continued on his way, never realizing that the faint light behind that door was illuminating far more than a small classroom.
It was lighting the path toward a new age.
Inside the room, the gathering was not discussing an ordinary university project, nor were they trying to solve another difficult mathematical equation.
Without realizing it, they were planting the very first seed of an idea that would one day transform the way humanity thinks, works, learns, and creates.
The hands of the clock moved quietly across the wall.
But history was racing forward.
And in that silent moment, no one heard the prophecy taking shape.
A prophecy that whispered the world would never be the same again...
That somewhere within a kingdom invisible to human eyes, a child not yet born would one day rise to bear a title known in every home, every classroom, every laboratory, and every city across the face of the Earth.
